From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 14:31:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: mfd: syscon: Add the Exynos9820 D-PHY top block

The bias generator of the Exynos9820 display D-PHY sits in a block of
its own, next to but outside the per link range. The SoC has room for a
second DSI controller, whose PHY would need the same block, so it is
described as a system controller the link nodes point at rather than as
a second register range in each of them.

Signed-off-by: Artur Szafraniec <ganggg111@gmail.com>
---
 Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
index e2286708806..e3303a93cd8 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/mfd/syscon.yaml
@@ -121,6 +121,7 @@ select:
           - rockchip,rk3576-qos
           - rockchip,rk3588-qos
           - rockchip,rv1126-qos
+          - samsung,exynos9820-dphy-top
           - st,spear1340-misc
           - stericsson,nomadik-pmu
           - starfive,jh7100-sysmain
@@ -235,6 +236,7 @@ properties:
               - rockchip,rk3576-qos
               - rockchip,rk3588-qos
               - rockchip,rv1126-qos
+              - samsung,exynos9820-dphy-top
               - st,spear1340-misc
               - stericsson,nomadik-pmu
               - starfive,jh7100-sysmain
